// ADDRESS-TRANSLATION-CANARY first slice: the mapping-authority contract the
// numeric page-table walk lacks (wiki/spec/resources/extents.md "Mapping and
// reclamation"). Cathedral's page-table package is the OS owner; Omega owns
// only the general authority and checking rules this boundary exercises.
//
// A translation provider installs and tears down mappings over ordinary
// extent custody. Fixed placement consumes the exact source and destination
// extents into one linear `Mapping` carrier that is only `Pending` after
// structural validation -- a pending mapping is not mapped access. The
// provider's activation crossing requalifies that same carrier `Installed`;
// only an installed mapping may be unmapped. `unmap` returns reusable
// `Granted` custody for both ranges plus the owed cross-core shootdown
// token -- TLB debt that must be discharged through `Shootdown::discharge`
// before the teardown is complete. Equal-length ranges are the contract's
// structural precondition, matching the conservation model's check.
//
// The borrowed-source route mirrors the owned one with different custody:
// `map_borrowed` takes a shared loan of the source while still consuming the
// destination, and the `BorrowedMapping` carrier keeps that loan visible so
// the lender's `Granted` source stays suspended -- it cannot be consumed,
// moved, or reclaimed while the mapping lives (matching
// `MappedExtent::loan_mut`'s refusal of mutable access under shared source
// custody in psi/foundation/extents). Releasing an installed borrowed
// mapping ends the loan instead of returning source custody: the lender's
// source qualification resumes, and teardown still owes the same shootdown.
//
// The obligation surface is source-spelled: `TranslationInstallObligations`
// and `TranslationReleaseObligations` are authored contract data, not just
// conservation-model internals. The caller authors the fact identities it
// requires, `map`/`map_borrowed` consume the sets into the carrier, and the
// carrier keeps them readable for its whole life -- the same surface the
// conservation model exposes as `install_obligations()`/
// `release_obligations()` on its grant, pending, installed, and teardown
// carriers. The sets are inert: holding or copying one grants no
// authority, and only the provider's activation and release receipt
// crossings discharge them. One carrier type keeps both sets across
// requalification where the model stages them per carrier; dropping a
// field at `activate` is not a spelling one type admits.
//
// The carrier also exposes the mapping's recorded geometry -- source and
// destination base and length as inert `addr`/`u64` fields minted by the
// `map` crossing, the same provider-visible surface the model's
// `PendingMap` offers as `source_base()`/`destination_base()` reads for
// deriving target translation entries. The values are provider-recorded
// evidence bound by the receipt crossings, not source-proven facts, and
// reading them grants no access: an address is data, not authority.
//
// Beside the contract sits `cathedral/`, the OS package's first surface
// carrying real page-table installation: a fully backed four-level
// hierarchy over qualified table extents, raw entry encoding, the level
// walk, and the hardware boundary requirements (entry store, root
// activation, leaf invalidation) its install/remove routes compose.
// `cathedral_install_and_teardown` drives the package against the exact
// pending mapping's recorded geometry: install through the walk, the
// activation receipt, leaf clear plus local invalidate, the release
// receipt, and the cross-core shootdown discharge. The package now also
// carries the second level of mapping authority: `install_huge`/
// `remove_huge` store and clear the terminal one level up, so a depth-2
// leaf maps the whole 2MiB span with no `pt` table -- granularity is the
// provider's install policy, and the authority's `Pending`/`Installed`/
// shootdown cycle is unchanged (`cathedral_huge_install_and_teardown`).
// The receipt crossings stay one-shot: replaying `activate` on an
// `Installed` carrier rejects
// (`tests/omega/fail/core/translation_double_activation`). Interpreting
// stored table memory is still the undeclared placed-access surface
// (wiki/spec/resources/placed_access.md), so the hardware crossings remain
// boundary requirements; demand-grown intermediate tables and multi-page
// installation are the package's next edges.
use omega::language::core::assembly;
use omega::language::core::extent;
use cathedral::hardware;
use cathedral::installer;

// One translation-activation fact an install receipt must establish,
// spelled as authored contract data. The identity is inert: naming a fact
// grants no authority, and nonzero normalization belongs to the provider's
// admission, not to source.
data TranslationActivationFact {
    identity: u64;
}

// One target-completion fact a release receipt must establish before the
// torn-down mapping's authority becomes reusable.
data TranslationCompletionFact {
    identity: u64;
}

// The exact install obligations a mapping binds, spelled as the authored
// fact identities the provider's activation receipt must cover. This
// contract fixes the set at two facts; a provider package's own contract
// declares the arity its receipts actually require.
data TranslationInstallObligations {
    facts: [TranslationActivationFact; 2];
}

// The exact release obligations a mapping binds, spelled as the authored
// fact identities the provider's release receipt must cover.
data TranslationReleaseObligations {
    facts: [TranslationCompletionFact; 2];
}

// Provider-owned identity of one pending or installed mapping over the
// exact consumed extents. Opaque to source: reconstructing or
// requalifying it outside the establishing routes below is not a spelling
// source can make.
boundary data MappingToken [linear];

// The owned-route carrier: an unforgeable provider identity beside the
// authored obligation sets the mapping binds. A consumer holding only the
// carrier still discovers the exact fact sets its activation or release
// receipt must establish. The geometry fields are the provider's recorded
// evidence for the consumed ranges -- the surface a provider reads to
// derive translation entries -- and carry no authority of their own.
data Mapping [linear] {
    token: MappingToken;
    source_base: addr;
    source_length: u64;
    destination_base: addr;
    destination_length: u64;
    install: TranslationInstallObligations;
    release: TranslationReleaseObligations;
}

domain Mapping::Pending
established by TranslationAuthority::map;

domain Mapping::Installed
established by TranslationAuthority::activate;

// Provider-owned identity of one borrowed-source mapping. Kept opaque for
// the same reason as `MappingToken`; the carrier below pairs it with the
// visible loan it holds, so source can never spell this token alone.
boundary data BorrowedMappingToken [linear];

// The borrowed-source carrier: an unforgeable provider identity, the
// visible shared loan of the lender's source, and the same authored
// obligation surface the owned route carries. While this value lives the
// loan stays active, which is what makes the lender's owned source
// unavailable until teardown releases the carrier.
data BorrowedMapping [linear] {
    token: BorrowedMappingToken;
    held_source: &Extent in Granted;
    source_base: addr;
    source_length: u64;
    destination_base: addr;
    destination_length: u64;
    install: TranslationInstallObligations;
    release: TranslationReleaseObligations;
}

domain BorrowedMapping::Pending
established by TranslationAuthority::map_borrowed;

domain BorrowedMapping::Installed
established by TranslationAuthority::activate_borrowed;

// The linear cross-core invalidation debt a teardown leaves. It cannot be
// dropped; only `discharge` consumes it.
boundary data Shootdown [linear];

domain Shootdown::Owed;

// Teardown's intermediate custody: the reusable destination, the owned
// source the mapping held, and the still-owed shootdown obligation.
data Unmapped {
    destination: Extent in Granted;
    source: Extent in Granted;
    shootdown: Shootdown in Owed;
}

// Borrowed teardown's intermediate custody has no `source` field: the loan
// ends when the carrier is consumed, so the lender -- not the unmap route --
// retains source authority. Only the destination and the shootdown debt
// return through the boundary.
data UnmappedBorrowed {
    destination: Extent in Granted;
    shootdown: Shootdown in Owed;
}

// The debt-free shape after `discharge`: both ranges' authority, nothing owed.
data Reclaimed {
    destination: Extent in Granted;
    source: Extent in Granted;
}

boundary trait TranslationAuthority {
    // Structural validation only: consumes the caller-authored obligation
    // sets into the pending carrier, where a consumer reads the exact fact
    // sets the provider's receipts must establish. The carrier holds both
    // ranges' custody and grants no mapped access.
    machine map(
        source: Extent in Granted,
        destination: Extent in Granted,
        install: TranslationInstallObligations,
        release: TranslationReleaseObligations
    ) -> Mapping
    requires
        source.length == destination.length
    ensures
        result in Mapping::Pending;

    // The provider receipt crossing: installed translations exist for the
    // exact pending mapping, and the carrier's authored install set is
    // what the receipt behind this edge must establish.
    machine activate(pending: Mapping in Pending) -> Mapping
    ensures
        result in Mapping::Installed;

    // Stale translations are released by the provider before this returns;
    // the carrier's authored release set is what that receipt must
    // establish, and the cross-core shootdown debt remains the caller's
    // to discharge.
    machine unmap(active: Mapping in Installed) -> Unmapped;

    // Structural validation over a shared source loan: the pending carrier
    // holds the loan, the destination's custody, and the caller-authored
    // obligation sets, and grants no mapped access. The lender's owned
    // source stays borrowed until release.
    machine map_borrowed(
        source: &Extent in Granted,
        destination: Extent in Granted,
        install: TranslationInstallObligations,
        release: TranslationReleaseObligations
    ) -> BorrowedMapping
    requires
        source.length == destination.length
    ensures
        result in BorrowedMapping::Pending;

    // The borrowed route's receipt crossing: installed translations exist
    // for the exact pending borrowed mapping.
    machine activate_borrowed(pending: BorrowedMapping in Pending)
        -> BorrowedMapping
    ensures
        result in BorrowedMapping::Installed;

    // Releasing an installed borrowed mapping ends the source loan; the
    // shootdown debt remains the caller's to discharge.
    machine unmap_borrowed(active: BorrowedMapping in Installed)
        -> UnmappedBorrowed;
}

boundary requirement Shootdown::discharge(self)
reaches MachineControl
requires
    self in Shootdown::Owed;

// The carrier-field reads the drivers exercise: a consumer holding only a
// pending or installed carrier still discovers the exact obligation sets
// its receipts must establish, matching `install_obligations()`/
// `release_obligations()` on the conservation model's carriers.
machine observe_install(obligations: &TranslationInstallObligations) {
}

machine observe_release(obligations: &TranslationReleaseObligations) {
}

// The Cathedral-shaped driver: install one owned mapping, then tear it down
// and discharge its TLB debt, recovering both ranges' authority.
machine install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> Reclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 1 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 7 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 2 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 9 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: Mapping in Pending =
        authority.map(source, destination, install, release);
    observe_install(&pending.install);
    let installed: Mapping in Installed = authority.activate(pending);
    observe_release(&installed.release);
    let unmapped: Unmapped = authority.unmap(installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = unmapped.source;
    Reclaimed { destination: released_destination, source: released_source }
}

// The borrowed-source driver: the provider borrows `source` for the life of
// the mapping while `destination` is consumed as before. Teardown ends the
// loan rather than returning a source, so the caller's own `source`
// authority is what resumes after the shootdown is discharged.
machine borrowed_install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> Reclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 3 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 4 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 5 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 6 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: BorrowedMapping in Pending =
        authority.map_borrowed(&source, destination, install, release);
    observe_install(&pending.install);
    let installed: BorrowedMapping in Installed =
        authority.activate_borrowed(pending);
    observe_release(&installed.release);
    let unmapped: UnmappedBorrowed = authority.unmap_borrowed(installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = source;
    Reclaimed { destination: released_destination, source: released_source }
}

// The Cathedral provider flow end to end: the pending carrier's recorded
// geometry feeds the package's real install -- the four-level walk, the
// entry stores, and the root activation -- before the authority's receipt
// crossing marks the mapping installed. Teardown runs the same pair in
// reverse: the package clears the leaf and invalidates the page's local
// translation, the release crossing returns both ranges' custody plus the
// owed shootdown, and `discharge` completes the cross-core debt.
machine cathedral_install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    hardware: &TranslationHardware,
    tables: &mut CathedralPageTables,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> Reclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + TranslationHardware + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 8 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 9 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 10 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 11 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: Mapping in Pending =
        authority.map(source, destination, install, release);
    tables.install(hardware, pending.source_base, pending.destination_base);
    let installed: Mapping in Installed = authority.activate(pending);
    tables.remove(hardware, installed.destination_base);
    let unmapped: Unmapped = authority.unmap(installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = unmapped.source;
    Reclaimed { destination: released_destination, source: released_source }
}

// The same provider flow at the second level of authority: a 2MiB leaf
// stored at depth 2. The mapping contract is granularity-agnostic -- the
// carrier records only ranges -- so the identical Pending -> Installed ->
// teardown sequence runs with the package's `install_huge`/`remove_huge`
// where the four-level driver used `install`/`remove`.
machine cathedral_huge_install_and_teardown(
    authority: &TranslationAuthority,
    hardware: &TranslationHardware,
    tables: &mut CathedralPageTables,
    source: Extent in Granted,
    destination: Extent in Granted
) -> Reclaimed
requires
    source.length == destination.length
reaches TranslationAuthority + TranslationHardware + MachineControl
{
    let install: TranslationInstallObligations = TranslationInstallObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 12 },
            TranslationActivationFact { identity: 13 }
        ],
    };
    let release: TranslationReleaseObligations = TranslationReleaseObligations {
        facts: [
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 14 },
            TranslationCompletionFact { identity: 15 }
        ],
    };
    let pending: Mapping in Pending =
        authority.map(source, destination, install, release);
    tables.install_huge(hardware, pending.source_base, pending.destination_base);
    let installed: Mapping in Installed = authority.activate(pending);
    tables.remove_huge(hardware, installed.destination_base);
    let unmapped: Unmapped = authority.unmap(installed);
    let owed: Shootdown in Owed = unmapped.shootdown;
    owed.discharge();
    let released_destination: Extent in Granted = unmapped.destination;
    let released_source: Extent in Granted = unmapped.source;
    Reclaimed { destination: released_destination, source: released_source }
}

data Main {
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) {
}
